        <body>
            <div xml:id="d571">

                <pb facs="0549" n="537" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg537"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.74/62: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Earle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-12-18T19:00:00+02:00">December 18,
                            1940—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>189. Ganovsky, Secretary of the Bulgarian Communist organization (illegal)
                    informs me that Soboleff asked the King for naval and air bases in Bulgaria.
                    Russia in return offered to force Turkey to give Adrianople and Turkish Thrace
                    to Bulgaria and to exert all possible pressure on Greece to cede Grecian Thrace
                    to the Kavala–Drama line.</p>
                <p>Ganovsky says that the King has courteously but firmly refused Russia’s
                    proposals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
